{"id": "EUVD-2026-86145", "enisaUuid": "928d81f9-cd2b-31d3-a6a8-6dd3c731698d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nregulator: tps6594: Fix device node reference leaks in multiphase loop\n\nIn tps6594_regulator_probe(), the multi-phase configuration loop calls\nof_find_node_by_name() to find buck nodes by name, and of_get_parent()\ntwice to navigate to the PMIC parent node. None of the acquired node\nreferences (np, intermediate parent, np_pmic_parent) are ever released\nvia of_node_put(), causing a reference leak on every loop iteration.\n\nAdditionally, of_find_node_by_name() can return NULL, but the result was\nimmediately passed to of_node_full_name() and of_get_parent() without a\nNULL check, which could lead to a NULL pointer dereference.\n\nFix this by:\n- Adding a NULL check for np after of_find_node_by_name()\n- Storing the intermediate parent node in a local variable np_parent\n- Calling of_node_put() on np, np_parent and np_pmic_parent at the\n  end of each loop iteration", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:52:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:08:27", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/28f70e0aa767a8f022c70ed75ecef227dc668121", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4a672bff99f6b58dde419fd12b3a53da137f032d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/68ce4f8223b78f8616ec7f4a02c38988eae627d2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fceac25487b21d6db940d2aed368e465d89cd1f4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7fd28093b3effc4f92566466df364622830ec608"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f775-wj9m-j2c6", "CVE-2026-93273"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "20cc0f36-2726-3498-ba6b-9431b6e3d227", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "36168342-cbe3-339f-8d81-f9586e076ad6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.5"}, {"id": "4675bd90-f03f-3700-9b92-df7cc957680f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "65608c70-29b1-3185-9971-3bf926b908d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f17ccc5deb4d024bb52fd3433471e77ab7ae9ad8 <4a672bff99f6b58dde419fd12b3a53da137f032d"}, {"id": "6ea4fada-bfa1-3d66-8523-995524d3365f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f17ccc5deb4d024bb52fd3433471e77ab7ae9ad8 <7fd28093b3effc4f92566466df364622830ec608"}, {"id": "6fa30e60-4710-3e4e-8d1c-2c268a10fdc1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7be99ec8-932a-3eb9-8dfd-15d273c2c0c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f17ccc5deb4d024bb52fd3433471e77ab7ae9ad8 <68ce4f8223b78f8616ec7f4a02c38988eae627d2"}, {"id": "996eb28f-2858-3597-91d8-fcd90289a27d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "9a30742a-30e7-32cb-b1e5-78fc006ffa22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f17ccc5deb4d024bb52fd3433471e77ab7ae9ad8 <fceac25487b21d6db940d2aed368e465d89cd1f4"}, {"id": "a69918cf-1f90-32dd-8df2-c8de01bb9926", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "a6e93808-6c84-3380-829f-85d71d31b66e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f17ccc5deb4d024bb52fd3433471e77ab7ae9ad8 <28f70e0aa767a8f022c70ed75ecef227dc668121"}, {"id": "f39b4684-984b-3836-98a2-68ca021c16db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f1ae7a66-8be9-3b6a-9abb-86e03c5af4e6", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}